<http://www.spektrix.com/nationalmusiccentre/event/180001ATQDMVSSRCQSPRRRJTDTKGSDVKD>
  a schema:Event;
  schema:name "NMC Presents: Jeremy Dutcher";
  schema:description """
	In honour of the National Day for Truth and Reconciliation , the National Music Centre presents an evening with Jeremy Dutcher. A Two-Spirit song carrier, composer, ethnomusicologist, and Wolastoqiyik member of Tobique First Nation, Dutcher is dedicated to language revitalization. <span><br/></span><span><br/></span>His award-winning music draws on archival recordings of his ancestors and is sung in Wolastoqey, his endangered mother tongue. Transcending boundaries, his work incorporates classical and jazz influences with reverence for the traditional songs of his home and the urgency of modern-day resistance. <span><br/></span><span><br/></span><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://www.google.com/maps/place/Studio+Bell,+home+of+the+National+Music+Centre/@51.0445506,-114.054786,17z/data=!3m1!4b1!4m5!3m4!1s0x53717aaa864fd43b:0x7609799479e4d20e!8m2!3d51.0445591!4d-114.0529828\">Studio Bell, 850 4 Street SE Calgary</a><span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Doors: 7:00 pm. Show: 8:00 pm.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>General Admission: $65.00 + GST<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span>NMC Members get 15% off. Log in with the email associated with your membership to automatically receive your discount.<span><br/></span>
""";
